IMPORT prelude

-- Health Records (Privacy and Access) Act 1997 (ACT) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- It uses only the built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH,
-- DATE_YEAR), not the daydate library. "Within n days after the day X" and "not later than n days after the day X" are
-- counted with the day X left out (Legislation Act 2001 (ACT) s 151, not deposited): the last day is X plus n. "2 weeks"
-- is 14 days and "1 week" is 7 days. A last day that falls on a weekend or public holiday is not moved (Legislation Act
-- s 151C, not deposited): NOTES.md, fork F2.
--
-- (c) Australian Capital Territory. Used under CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md). Unofficial text.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Health Records (Privacy and Access) Act 1997`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

-- The day n days after a day (n may be negative: n days before).
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `plus days` n MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS n)

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

-- Whether the first day is strictly before the second.
GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE, `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first` `falls before` `the second` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second`

-- The later of two days.
GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE, `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of` `the first` `and` `the second` MEANS IF `the first` `falls before` `the second` THEN `the second` ELSE `the first`

-- Whether a year is a leap year (Gregorian rule).
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a leap year` y IF
        (y MODULO 4 EQUALS 0 AND (NOT (y MODULO 100 EQUALS 0)))
    OR  y MODULO 400 EQUALS 0

-- The same day n years later ("the day the consumer turns 25", "7 years after the day"). A 29 February with no
-- 29 February in the later year is taken as 1 March (NOTES.md, fork F3).
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `plus years` n MEANS
    IF DATE_DAY `the day` EQUALS 29 AND DATE_MONTH `the day` EQUALS 2 AND (NOT (`is a leap year` (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS n)))
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS n)
    ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY (DATE_DAY `the day`) (DATE_MONTH `the day`) (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS n)
